{%- comment -%}
  Fixed 5-item nav (Home / New In / Shop / About Us / Seen In) —
  intentionally ignores the store's main-menu link list. About Us /
  New In / Seen In URLs come from the header section's settings
  (theme editor), since they can't be known from theme code. Shop
  links to /collections — the family picker page
  (sections/pm-shop-browse), not the product grid — that used to only
  exist as a hover/click dropdown here. Picking a family there goes on
  to that family's actual products at /collections/all?family=....
  Seen In links to the Press page (sections/pm-press.liquid, rendered
  for page.handle == 'press').
{%- endcomment -%}
<ul class="site-nav site-navigation small--hide">
  <li class="site-nav__item site-nav__expanded-item">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="site-nav__link site-nav__link--underline">Home</a>
  </li>
  <li class="site-nav__item site-nav__expanded-item">
    <a href="{{ collections['aw27'].url | default: aw27_url | default: '/collections/aw27' }}" class="site-nav__link site-nav__link--underline">New In</a>
  </li>
  <li class="site-nav__item site-nav__expanded-item">
    <a href="{{ routes.collections_url | default: '/collections' }}" class="site-nav__link site-nav__link--underline">Shop</a>
  </li>
  <li class="site-nav__item site-nav__expanded-item">
    {%- comment -%}
      pages['about-us'].url first, not the setting -- it's resolved
      fresh for the current request's locale (and any translated
      handle), where a hardcoded/picked path like "/pages/about-us"
      stays pinned to whatever locale it was saved under and opens the
      wrong page when browsing the storefront in Italian. The setting
      is still honored when no such page exists, for merchants who
      deliberately point "About Us" somewhere else.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="{{ pages['about-us'].url | default: about_us_url | default: '/pages/about-us' }}" class="site-nav__link site-nav__link--underline">About Us</a>
  </li>
  <li class="site-nav__item site-nav__expanded-item">
    <a href="{{ pages['press'].url | default: press_url | default: '/pages/press' }}" class="site-nav__link site-nav__link--underline">Seen In</a>
  </li>
</ul>
